ent :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329477}] :question/math-academy-id "q-47380" :question/problem "The function $g(s)$ describes the amount of fuel, in liters, remaining in Samuel's car after driving $s$ miles. The values of $g(s)$ for different values of $s$ are given in the table below:\n\n| $s$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ | $10$ | $12$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(s)$ | $15$ | $13.5$ | $12.1$ | $9.4$ | $8.2$ | $6.6$ | $4.8$ |\n\nApproximate the rate of change in the fuel volume when $s=8$ miles using a forward difference approximation."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317198 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315767} :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316998}] :question/math-academy-id "q-342038" :question/problem "The volume of water in a tank was recorded over time for $25$ minutes, starting from time $t=0$ minutes. The following table shows the volume $V(t)$, in liters, recorded at time $t.$\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $5$ | $10$ | $15$ | $20$ | $25$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $V(t)$ | $120$ | $150$ | $165$ | $180$ | $215$ | $240$ |\n\nApproximate the rate of change of volume at time $t=5$ using a forward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\nAt $t=5,$ the estimated rate of change is {{field-1}} liters per minute."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317199 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "110" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "110" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315489} :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316834}] :question/math-academy-id "q-342040" :question/problem "A hiker’s elevation was recorded over time for $6$ hours, starting from time $t=0$ hours. The following table shows the elevation $E(t)$, in meters, recorded at time $t.$\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $E(t)$ | $0$ | $200$ | $310$ | $395$ | $450$ | $525$ | $600$ |\n\nApproximate the rate of change of elevation at time $t=1$ using a forward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\nAt $t=1,$ the estimated rate of change is {{field-1}} meters per hour."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329811 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328036} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328247} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328268} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328686} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.5\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328956}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328036} :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329424}] :question/math-academy-id "q-47378" :question/problem "Andrey wants to estimate his running speed. Andrey's friend Max takes note of Andrey's position while he is on the track. Max's observations are given in the table below, where $s(t)$ is the distance covered, measured in meters, $t$ seconds after Andrey started running.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $s(t)$ | $0$ | $4$ | $9$ | $15$ | $20$ | $27$ |\n\nApproximate Andrey's speed at t